","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Matt O'Sullivan","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10958","person_slug":"matt-osullivan","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Mehreen Faruqi","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10912","person_slug":"mehreen-faruqi","vote":"no"},{"name":"Murray Watt","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10857","person_slug":"murray-watt","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Nick McKim","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10841","person_slug":"nick-mckim","vote":"no"},{"name":"Patrick Dodson","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10846","person_slug":"patrick-dodson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Paul Scarr","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10949","person_slug":"paul-scarr","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Penny Wong","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10678","person_slug":"penny-wong","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Perin Davey","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10947","person_slug":"perin-davey","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"no"},{"name":"Raff Ciccone","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10915","person_slug":"raff-ciccone","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Rex Patrick","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10903","person_slug":"rex-patrick","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sam McMahon","party":"Country Liberal Party","person_id":"tvfy_10948","person_slug":"sam-mcmahon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Henderson","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10790","person_slug":"sarah-henderson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Slade Brockman","party":"DPRES","person_id":"tvfy_10900","person_slug":"slade-brockman","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stirling Griff","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10851","person_slug":"stirling-griff","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Susan McDonald","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10951","person_slug":"susan-mcdonald","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tim Ayres","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10946","person_slug":"tim-ayres","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Sheldon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10944","person_slug":"tony-sheldon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Wendy Askew","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10914","person_slug":"wendy-askew","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Security Legislation Amendment (Critical Infrastructure Protection) Bill 2022 - Third Reading - Pass the bill","noes":8,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2022-03-30.229.1) to [pass the bill](https://peo.gov.au/understand-our-parliament/how-parliament-works/bills-and-laws/making-a-law-in-the-australian-parliament/) in the Senate. The bill will now be sent back to the House of Representatives where our MPs will consider whether they agree with Senate amendments. ### What does the bill do? According to the [bill homepage](https://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id:legislation/billhome/r6833), the purpose of the bill is to: * *provide that specified critical infrastructure assets must adopt and maintain a critical infrastructure risk management program;* * *provide for annual reporting obligations for assets that are exempt from the risk management program obligation;* * *make minor amendments in relation to consultation requirements and immunities;* * *provide for additional cyber security obligations that may be applied in relation to systems of national significance;* * *provide that directions facilitating government assistance to industry in the event of a serious cyber security incident prevail over the requirements of a risk management program;* * *amend provisions that authorise the use and disclosure of protected information;* * *provide that the minister's power to privately declare an asset as a critical infrastructure asset includes a power to require compliance with a risk management program; and* * *enable the minister to declare a critical infrastructure asset to be a system of national of significance; and include additional reporting requirements.* See the [bills digest](https://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/bd/bd2122a/22bd055) for more detailed information.","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-7685","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2022-03-30/13"}
